Ceres shell. Type 'help' for the commands.
ceres:/> Commands:
  help [command]     what the commands do
  ls [dir]           the files and directories in a directory
  cd [dir]           go to a directory (/ alone: the top)
  cat <file>...      show what a file holds
  run <file> [args]  run a program (.cres), then come back here
  clear              clear the screen
  mem                how much memory there is, and how much free
  time               the date and time, and how long since start
  info               what this machine is
  reset              start the machine again
  exit [status]      leave the shell, and the machine stops
A program can also be run by its name alone: snake, or snake.cres.
Up and Down bring back earlier lines.
ceres:/> cd [dir]
  go to a directory (/ alone: the top)
ceres:/> docs/                       <dir>
games/                      <dir>
top.txt                         4
ceres:/> readme.txt                     32
ceres:/> top.txt                         4
ceres:/> ceres:/games> docs/                       <dir>
games/                      <dir>
top.txt                         4
ceres:/games> greet: [games/greet.cres] [3] [two] PWD=/games
(exit status 3)
ceres:/games> greet: [games/greet.cres] [0] PWD=/games
ceres:/games> ceres:/> ceres:/docs> Hello from a file.
Second line.
